good@x = fraction of the 40 samples in which a lambda-MAP at lambda = x is the true parity (any rate).
right neighbour: family of the lambda-MAP just below tau_n (C = parity + rule cells, E = named inputs,
D = envelope); 'none' = the good model is not a lambda-MAP for any lambda in that sample.
